//? Title: CenterNet Gaussian centres and learned upsampling
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Verify Gaussian radii, maximum-combined heatmaps, centre collisions and analytic loss derivatives, then check the full learned-upsample graph and explicitly fit the complete compact source detector with paired BN checkpoints.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.6_object_detection/centernet.cpp`.

> The method

CenterNet detects objects as class heatmap centres with learned size and subpixel offsets. Size-adaptive Gaussians supervise peak location, while masked L1 supervises geometric attributes at retained centres.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/centernet_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/centernet_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/centernet_concept.tikz > build/centernet_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/centernet_concept.svg build/centernet_concept.dvi > build/centernet_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
