> Full learned-upsample graph and compact fit

The full ResNet18 CenterNet has 14,046,164 learned and 10,496 BN-state scalars.
Three 4x4 stride-two transposed convolutions (256/128/64 channels) each have
BN/ReLU. Independent 3x3/ReLU then1x1 heads predict 80 heatmaps, height/width
and dy/dx. Head kernels use normal standard deviation .001, heatmap bias -2.19;
encoder/deconvolutions use their source initialization. No pretrained weights
are loaded. This full128-pixel backward verifies all81 learned tensor derivatives.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  n::ParameterStore p(17), state(17);
  n::models::CenterNetConfig c;
  c.update_stats = false;
  const auto net = n::models::CenterNet(
      p, state, n::sin(.13 * n::arange(0, 128 * 128 * 3)).reshape({1, 128, 128, 3}), c, true);
  if (p.count() != 14046164 || state.count() != 10496 ||
      net.heatmap.shape() != n::Shape{1, 32, 32, 80})
    return 1;
  const auto g = n::grad(n::mean(n::square(net.heatmap)) + n::mean(n::square(net.size)) +
                             n::mean(n::square(net.offset)),
                         p.parameters());
  if (g.size() != 81)
    return 1;
  for (const auto &v : g)
    if (!v.defined() || !std::isfinite(n::sum(n::square(v)).item()))
      return 1;
  std::print("Full CenterNet128: {} learned/{} state scalars,32x32x80 heatmap and all{} "
             "finite defined learned tensor derivatives. Initialized validation, not trained "
             "benchmark output.\n",
             p.count(), state.count(), g.size());
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Full CenterNet128: 14046164 learned/10496 state scalars,32x32x80 heatmap and all81 finite defined learned tensor derivatives. Initialized validation, not trained benchmark output.
// result_end

The complete compact source network uses ResNet18 with widths divided by
eight, upsampling widths64/32/32 and hidden heads32: 319,862 learned and1,456
BN-state scalars. This report fits64-pixel scenes, an explicit smaller-scene
adaptation. The split uses64 fit/16 validation scenes from the first2048
MNIST training digits(seed11), and eight test scenes from the first512 official
test digits(seed22). Actual training pixels and boxes appear below.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/centernet_scenes.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::set_num_threads(2);

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";
  dm::datasets::fetch("mnist", (cache / "mnist").string());

  const auto train = n::load_mnist((cache / "mnist").string(), "train");
  n::models::DetectionSceneConfig cfg;
  cfg.scenes = 80;
  cfg.seed = 11;
  const auto scenes = n::models::MakeTensorDetectionScenes(
      n::slice_axis(train.images, 0, 0, 2048), n::slice_axis(train.labels, 0, 0, 2048), cfg);

  std::vector<n::Tensor> boxes(scenes.boxes.begin(), scenes.boxes.begin() + 8);
  const auto preview = n::models::DrawDetectionBoxes(n::slice_axis(scenes.images, 0, 0, 8),
                                                     boxes, {.1, 1., .2});
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(preview, "build/centernet_scenes.png", 4, 0., 1., 4, 1., 2);
  std::int64_t objects = 0;
  for (const auto &b : scenes.boxes)
    objects += b.shape()[0];
  std::print("80 generated training/validation scenes; {} accepted digits. Preview: first "
             "eight training scenes with tight green boxes.\n",
             objects);
}
