\image(figures/centernet_detections.png)
\caption(Actual restored compact CenterNet detections in red, with green true boxes on eight held-out scenes. Incorrect sizes, extra peaks and class errors remain visible.)
\alttext(Eight held-out digit scenes showing true boxes and CenterNet peak-decoded predictions.)

> Conclusion

The selected epoch26 has validation AP50 .066967. Test AP50 is .025192, AP75 is zero and AP50:95 is .007186, with 800 detections. This bounded schedule generalizes poorly despite decreasing training loss; extra/mislocalized boxes remain visible.

Independent Gaussian and objective oracles precede full-graph validation and explicit compact fitting. The selected learned and normalization state are restored together; actual held-out predictions illustrate this instructional run without claiming full-dataset accuracy.

> References

- [Zhou, Wang and Krähenbühl (2019), Objects as Points](https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.07850).
- [Authors’ Gaussian radius and heatmap implementation](https://github.com/xingyizhou/CenterNet/blob/master/src/lib/utils/image.py).
